WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.440
Hi, welcome back to the Lam Rim.

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.050
Boy, what's this lady
about, why is she so grumpy?

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:09.300
Okay, we're going to talk
about that. Here we go.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:13.102
SKYE DKA' BA RNAMS LA
DMIGS SU BKAR TE BSGOM

00:00:13.102 --> 00:00:18.102
SKYE DKA' BA means difficult to generate

00:00:18.214 --> 00:00:21.272
and guess what it means, you guys?

00:00:21.272 --> 00:00:23.642
That lady?

00:00:23.642 --> 00:00:25.252
What are we on?

00:00:25.252 --> 00:00:27.493
We're on compassion.

00:00:27.493 --> 00:00:29.725
[TL] Generate responsibility.

00:00:29.725 --> 00:00:33.028
[GMR] Well, we didn't reach
quite there yet, but okay.

00:00:33.028 --> 00:00:35.960
So if there's people in your life

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:40.030
that you have a lot of trouble
feeling empathy with them.

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:43.410
They are just so irritating that, look,

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.722
I know you're suffering
but I don't really care

00:00:45.722 --> 00:00:47.605
because you're so irritating.

00:00:47.605 --> 00:00:50.870
So if there's difficult
people in your life

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:54.130
to feel empathy with, then DMIGS SU BKAR.

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:56.993
DMIGS SU BKAR is an
idiom, difficult idiom.

00:00:56.993 --> 00:01:00.410
BKAR has many different meanings,

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:04.927
but DMIGS SU BKAR means take
them as a separate focus group.

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:08.350
Take all the assholes in your life

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:11.043
and take them as a separate focus group

00:01:11.043 --> 00:01:12.243
and focus on them.

00:01:12.243 --> 00:01:15.750
DMIGS SU BKAR BA means separate
them out from your life,

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:19.840
all the difficult people,
put them in a special group

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:21.950
and try to get empathy for them.

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:23.997
Work on your empathy for them.

00:01:23.997 --> 00:01:26.330
TSANGS PA SOGS LA SKYE DKA' NA

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:30.560
SKYES BU 'BRING GI SKABS
LTAR BSAMS PAS SKYE BA 'ONG

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:34.010
TSANGS PA SOGS here means
Brahma, like worldly god,

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:37.618
like Superman, or Iron
Man, or Wonder Woman.

00:01:37.618 --> 00:01:42.290
But the point is, if
there are powerful people,

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:45.113
like powerful politicians,

00:01:47.368 --> 00:01:52.340
who you have difficulty
feeling compassion for them

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:57.163
because they are so unkind
or they are so crude people.

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:01.800
And if you feel difficulty, SKYE DKA' NA,

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:04.970
if you have difficulty
feeling empathy for them

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:09.540
then go back to the lower
sections of the Lam Rim,

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:13.490
medium capacity people. Think about, look,

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:17.160
they're also in a body,
their body also hurts,

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:19.360
they also have relationship problems,

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:21.143
they also have financial problems.

00:02:21.143 --> 00:02:25.000
Half the rich people in the
world are broke, trust me.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:29.840
They are just living on huge
debts and they're nervous

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:31.660
and they have family problems.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:33.180
They have health problems.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:35.810
They definitely have
mental health problems.

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:40.800
And try to have some empathy
for those difficult people

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:41.933
in your life.

00:02:41.933 --> 00:02:44.530
You have trouble feeling
compassion for them,

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:49.100
try to go back to the medium
Lam Rim and think about

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:51.560
the sufferings that we were
supposed to think about

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:55.093
for ourselves and apply
it to those people.

00:02:56.486 --> 00:02:59.200
SNYING RJE CHEN PO RGYUD
LA SKYES PA'I TSAD NI

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:03.490
This TSAD has been very
useful throughout this section

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:07.440
of the Lam Rim in the seven step process

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:11.910
for reaching bodhichitta
or bodhisattva's vision.

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:14.300
What's TSAD Tim?

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:17.890
Yeah, how do you know when you got it?

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:21.122
And that's so useful, like how do you know

00:03:21.122 --> 00:03:23.230
when you reach compassion,

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:25.690
and you can go on to put responsibility?

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:30.140
How do you know when
you reach number five?

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:33.880
And because it's so difficult
to quantify emotions,

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:37.120
it's so difficult to say,
"Okay, Tim, now you got love,

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:39.340
you didn't have love yesterday
and today you have it."

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:42.212
It's so difficult to put a number on it.

00:03:42.212 --> 00:03:45.452
So how do you put a number
on compassion? TSAD NI,

00:03:45.452 --> 00:03:49.745
SEMS CAN THAMS CAD SDUG BSNGAL
DANG BRAL 'DOD AA MAS BU

00:03:49.745 --> 00:03:52.303
GCES PA NAD DRAG PO LTA BU'I SDUG BSNGAL

00:03:52.303 --> 00:03:54.930
CAN ZHIG LA SEMS PA BZHIN

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:58.190
When you have this emotion,

00:03:58.190 --> 00:04:02.610
like a mother trying to eat
breakfast, while her child

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:06.340
is in the hospital recovering
from a car accident

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:10.310
in which they were almost killed.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:12.232
So imagine you're a mom.

00:04:12.232 --> 00:04:14.133
Here's a picture.

00:04:14.133 --> 00:04:17.860
You're a mom, your kid
got in a car accident.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:22.002
The kid is in the hospital
fighting for their life, and

00:04:22.002 --> 00:04:26.640
you're having breakfast. You're
sitting there having coffee.

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:28.895
By the way, she looks too happy.

00:04:28.895 --> 00:04:32.930
I'm sorry, I should have found a more...

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:37.060
Anyway, this lady's only
child got almost killed

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:40.780
in a car accident and the
child's in the hospital

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:44.300
struggling for her life or his life,

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:47.090
and then she's having coffee.

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:49.990
But what is she really doing?

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:52.260
She's only thinking about the child.

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:54.767
Her mind is totally
obsessed with the child.

00:04:54.767 --> 00:04:57.240
Okay, she has to eat. She has to drink.

00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:00.860
She does, parents of kids who are dying

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:03.900
still have breakfast, but during breakfast

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:06.400
you can bet they are not
thinking about breakfast.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:09.125
So when you reach this point,

00:05:09.125 --> 00:05:12.113
BZA' BTUNG GI TSE TSUN CHAD

00:05:12.113 --> 00:05:15.562
BZA' BTUNG means while
you're eating your breakfast,

00:05:15.562 --> 00:05:18.855
food and drink, and you're still

00:05:18.855 --> 00:05:21.990
having thoughts of empathy
about all the other people

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:25.602
in the world having the same
problems at the same moment.

00:05:25.602 --> 00:05:29.570
When you reach that point
then you have compassion.

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:32.850
When you can't even during breakfast,

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:36.310
you can't eat a croissant
without being a little bit

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:40.227
distracted about all the
people dying this morning,

00:05:40.227 --> 00:05:42.343
then you have compassion.

00:05:42.343 --> 00:05:44.480
Then you got it.

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:48.350
As much as a mom would
have for her only child

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:51.065
who's in the hospital
struggling for their life

00:05:51.065 --> 00:05:54.290
at that moment. And that,
boy, that's a high bar.

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:56.933
That's a really high bar.

00:05:56.933 --> 00:05:59.470
That's a high TSAD.

00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:01.597
All right.

00:06:01.597 --> 00:06:04.863
DE YANG SDUG BSNGAL LAS BRAL
'DOD TZAM GYI SNYING RJE NI,

00:06:04.863 --> 00:06:07.580
NYAN RANG DANG THUN MONG
BA'I SNYING RJE YIN LA

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:10.540
Now he's going to talk about
two kinds of compassion

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:12.370
and two kinds of love.

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:14.760
Okay, we were just struggling

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:17.440
with what's the difference
between love and compassion.

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:22.080
Basically, love is the desire
that people have happiness,

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:23.640
and compassion is the desire

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:25.650
that people don't have suffering,

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:28.890
and there's a debate about
which one should come first.

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:32.960
And to help us with that
debate, Pabongka Rinpoche

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:37.160
is going to split love into two types

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:40.900
and he's going to split
compassion into two types.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:45.872
And this is not one of
those Gelugpa Tsongkapian,

00:06:45.872 --> 00:06:47.700
oh, they just like to make divisions

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:49.170
and more outlines.

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:51.230
It's not really that.

00:06:51.230 --> 00:06:55.760
It's that the more subtleties
you learn about compassion,

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:58.910
the easier it will be
for you to develop it.

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:03.010
If you learn several colors of compassion

00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:07.340
then you will be better
able to master compassion.

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:10.610
So we're going to talk about
two kinds of compassion here.

00:07:11.727 --> 00:07:16.727
First one is SDUG BSNGAL LAS
BRAL 'DOD GYI SNYING RJE,

00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:19.330
which means

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:21.768
you want to pull people out of the fire.

00:07:21.768 --> 00:07:24.260
People fell in the fire
and you're obsessed

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:26.880
with getting them out of the fire.

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:30.520
You're obsessed with pulling
them out of suffering.

00:07:30.520 --> 00:07:31.995
That's the first one.

00:07:31.995 --> 00:07:34.161
The second flavor of compassion is...

00:07:34.161 --> 00:07:36.087
and oh by the way he says,

00:07:36.087 --> 00:07:40.230
"Non-bodhisattvas do have this
first kind of compassion."

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:44.720
So people who didn't reach
bodhisattva vision yet,

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:47.680
like lower track people,

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:49.680
self-made buddhas and listeners,

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:52.550
they still have this
motivation that they don't like

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:54.123
to see people suffering.

00:07:54.123 --> 00:07:56.190
That's part of all Buddhist practice.

00:07:56.190 --> 00:07:58.300
You don't have to be a bodhisattva

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:01.470
to be concerned about
other people's suffering.

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:06.040
But the second one, SDUG
BSNGAL LAS SKYOB 'DOD,

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:09.703
by the way, heavy prenasal
traditionally here.

00:08:10.623 --> 00:08:14.230
SKYOB 'DOD say, SKYOB 'DOD.

00:08:14.230 --> 00:08:16.831
It's really SKYOB 'DOD,

00:08:16.831 --> 00:08:20.320
but there's a tradition to
pronounce it SKYOB 'DOD.

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:24.400
And SKYOB 'DOD means you want to %BSKYAB.

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:26.340
You want to protect that person.

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:30.560
So there's a slight difference in accent.

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:33.910
The first one just wants to
pull them out of the fire.

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:37.470
The second one is jump in
front of the fire and, yeah,

00:08:37.470 --> 00:08:38.900
protect them from the fire.

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:41.530
It's a slight difference.

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:44.780
First one you don't have to
be a bodhisattva to have it.

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:49.163
The second one leads to
having bodhisattva vision,

00:08:49.163 --> 00:08:50.460
bodhichitta.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:54.100
So if you have this
big desire to wrap them

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:58.930
in your arms, in addition to
throwing them out of that fire

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:00.470
and you want to protect
them from the fire,

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:04.400
and presumably, even at your own expense,

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:07.849
maybe you take some of the pain yourself.

00:09:07.849 --> 00:09:10.070
That's a higher kind of compassion

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:14.660
and only the bodhisattva
track people have that.

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:17.148
THEG CHEN THUN MONG MA YIN PA

00:09:17.148 --> 00:09:20.657
That's unique to the Greater Way.

00:09:20.657 --> 00:09:24.210
PHYI MA 'DI BSKYED PAR BYED,
therefore we are working

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:26.630
to get to the second one,

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:28.970
he says. PHYI MA means the second one,

00:09:28.970 --> 00:09:31.603
we're working on the second one.

00:09:31.603 --> 00:09:34.260
DES NA, 'DI DAG SKYE DKA' YANG

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:39.010
Oh, I sent a picture of a, I
was thinking of an umbrella.

00:09:41.150 --> 00:09:46.150
This idea of taking refuge or
this idea of taking shelter.

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:52.310
I think umbrellas are nice
metaphors for taking refuge.

00:09:52.310 --> 00:09:55.633
It's raining and not only

00:09:57.460 --> 00:10:02.460
do you want to pull your
own child out of the rain,

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:05.290
but you have an umbrella ready for them.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:07.250
It's a different thing.

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:09.870
You're ready to keep them dry,

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:13.730
not just to get them out of the wet.

00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:16.320
So that's bodhisattva motivation.

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:19.787
DES NA, 'DI DAG SKYE
DKA' YANG SKYE THABS LA

00:10:19.787 --> 00:10:22.190
BRTZON PA CHEN PO BSKYED DE 'BAD DGOS

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:25.030
Look, the second one's harder

00:10:25.030 --> 00:10:28.860
because it starts to shade
into taking responsibility

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:32.280
for these people if you have the umbrella.

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:36.617
So you can feel how he's
taking us to the next step

00:10:37.755 --> 00:10:39.790
in developing bodhichitta.

00:10:39.790 --> 00:10:43.120
He's saying you should
have your umbrella ready

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:45.980
and what's he going to say next?

00:10:45.980 --> 00:10:49.000
Then you should LHAG BSAM

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:52.100
Then you should take responsibility.

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:54.530
I carried an umbrella
around in my backpack.

00:10:54.530 --> 00:10:56.780
Okay, why is that backpack so heavy?

00:10:56.780 --> 00:11:00.130
I have an umbrella in there, I used to.

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:04.260
I carried it around for years in Arizona.

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:06.870
It doesn't rain in Arizona.

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:10.070
And then we went to see
the people at Google

00:11:10.070 --> 00:11:15.070
to talk about Tibetan
translation and it poured,

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:18.340
and I pulled it out and I said, yay!

00:11:18.340 --> 00:11:21.060
Scott and Orit were with
me and we all were--

00:11:21.060 --> 00:11:23.980
Scott was not so dry but
me and Orit were dry.

00:11:23.980 --> 00:11:26.480
But you know, you're ready.

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:28.346
All right.

00:11:29.842 --> 00:11:34.000
SNGAR RANG NYID NA MYONG BA'I

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.229
NA MYONG BA

00:11:35.229 --> 00:11:38.610
means if you have
experienced a certain kind of

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:41.565
disease, illness,

00:11:41.565 --> 00:11:46.028
NAD DRAG PO if you've
had a serious illness,

00:11:46.028 --> 00:11:48.020
like when I was studying in India,

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:49.970
I got what do you call it?

00:11:49.970 --> 00:11:52.960
Hepatitis, yeah.

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:54.510
I was in bed for a month

00:11:54.510 --> 00:11:58.210
and I couldn't get out of bed for a month.

00:11:58.210 --> 00:12:01.740
And I recovered. There
is a Tibetan medicine,

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:05.373
by the way, and I recovered fine.

00:12:06.502 --> 00:12:10.050
But after that I had a
special place in my heart

00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:14.830
for people who got hepatitis.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:17.515
So every time I heard
somebody got hepatitis,

00:12:17.515 --> 00:12:19.850
I'm like yeah, I know,
man, I've been there.

00:12:19.850 --> 00:12:22.290
You know, I had that.

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:25.190
I know how you feel to
lay in bed for a month.

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:27.330
I know how you feel.

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:29.520
So there's a kind of super empathy.

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:33.790
He says here, NA MYONG BA'I NAD DRAG PO

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:37.026
If you have experienced a
serious illness yourself,

00:12:37.026 --> 00:12:39.884
DE 'DRA ZHIG MI GZHAN NA BA MTHONG NA

00:12:39.884 --> 00:12:42.950
if you see another person
with that same disease,

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:46.309
RANG NYID KYI MYONG BA
RGYU MTSAN DU BYAS NAS

00:12:46.309 --> 00:12:51.309
taking your previous personal
experience as a foundation,

00:12:51.513 --> 00:12:55.520
SNYING RJE SKYE, you're
able to get compassion.

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:58.970
If you can relate to
something you had before

00:12:58.970 --> 00:13:01.540
you're more compassionate towards people

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:03.828
who have the same disease.

00:13:03.828 --> 00:13:06.903
SKYES BU CHUNG 'BRING GI SKABS
SU 'KHOR BA DANG NGAN SONG GI

00:13:06.903 --> 00:13:09.402
SDUG BSNGAL RANG STENG DU
LEGS PAR BSGOMS PA RNAMS

00:13:09.402 --> 00:13:12.550
Therefore, if you have
done the first ten years

00:13:12.550 --> 00:13:16.190
of the Lam Rim well, and during the

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:19.720
person of lesser capacity

00:13:19.720 --> 00:13:22.500
and the person of medium capacity steps,

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:25.990
you worked hard on
understanding all the suffering

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:28.170
you've had in your many lifetimes,

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:31.668
it's going to be easier
for you to have compassion

00:13:31.668 --> 00:13:33.560
because you're already thinking

00:13:33.560 --> 00:13:37.460
about all the times
you had those diseases.

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:41.410
So therefore, people who
get to the bodhisattva...

00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:45.090
Why don't we start Lam Rim
at the bodhisattva section

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:47.420
of the Lam Rim is because first

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:49.717
you have to get sick yourself.

00:13:49.717 --> 00:13:52.010
First, you have to go through
that disease yourself.

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:55.740
You have to be aware,
sensitive, to how you have had

00:13:55.740 --> 00:13:58.660
all those problems yourself
in the lower realms,

00:13:58.660 --> 00:14:01.130
with your previous marriages,

00:14:01.130 --> 00:14:02.970
et cetera, et cetera.

00:14:02.970 --> 00:14:05.050
If you've been through
all those sufferings

00:14:05.050 --> 00:14:08.060
then you reach the bodhisattva
section of the Lam Rim,

00:14:08.060 --> 00:14:12.400
you're ready to say,
Oh, I had that before.

00:14:12.400 --> 00:14:14.140
I had that disease before.

00:14:14.140 --> 00:14:16.190
I had the same thing with my ex-wife.

00:14:16.190 --> 00:14:17.660
Yeah I understand,

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:20.520
or ex-husband.

00:14:23.302 --> 00:14:26.060
And in that sense, studying the Lam Rim

00:14:26.060 --> 00:14:28.040
is like laying bricks.

00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:31.340
Studying the Lam Rim is very similar

00:14:31.340 --> 00:14:35.130
to laying courses of bricks.

00:14:35.130 --> 00:14:38.260
You can see here,

00:14:38.260 --> 00:14:42.720
those lower levels of brick,

00:14:42.720 --> 00:14:45.990
where the cement has dried already,

00:14:45.990 --> 00:14:50.990
that's the steps of the path
for people of lesser capacity

00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:55.280
and steps of the path for
people of medium capacity,

00:14:55.280 --> 00:15:00.010
where we thought a lot
about our own troubles.

00:15:00.010 --> 00:15:03.350
And that's like having hepatitis before.

00:15:03.350 --> 00:15:07.190
Then when you reach this new
level that he's building now,

00:15:07.190 --> 00:15:11.040
or she, and you're building
the bodhisattva levels

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:12.530
of the Lam Rim,

00:15:12.530 --> 00:15:15.740
because you did a good
job in the medium level

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:18.490
of the Lam Rim and the
lesser levels of the Lam Rim,

00:15:18.490 --> 00:15:22.920
your bodhisattva house is
going to be much stronger.

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:30.710
Now we talked about two
kinds of compassion.

00:15:30.710 --> 00:15:34.390
He divided compassion into
sort of a lower compassion,

00:15:34.390 --> 00:15:37.370
where you just want to
pull people out of the fire

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:40.690
and then a higher kind of
compassion where you want

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:42.980
to kind of hug them and protect them

00:15:42.980 --> 00:15:45.340
from the fire and pull them out.

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:48.210
And now we're going to
get a similar distinction

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:50.900
in BYAMS PA, in love.

00:15:50.900 --> 00:15:54.270
So there's two kinds of love,
which are kind of parallel

00:15:54.270 --> 00:15:56.611
to those two kinds of compassion.

00:15:56.611 --> 00:16:00.310
And again, it's not just BS,

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:02.828
a new category for the text

00:16:02.828 --> 00:16:04.428
or something like that.

00:16:04.428 --> 00:16:06.713
It's if you go deeper,

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:11.770
your experience of love and
compassion can go deeper.

00:16:11.770 --> 00:16:13.241
So here we go.

00:16:13.241 --> 00:16:17.020
SEMS CAN LA GCES SHING PHANGS
PA'I YID 'ONG GI BYAMS PA

00:16:17.020 --> 00:16:19.310
We talked about beautiful love,

00:16:19.310 --> 00:16:22.940
where you feel attracted to people.

00:16:22.940 --> 00:16:26.110
When you're around people, you feel like

00:16:27.810 --> 00:16:30.730
someone just gave you a
hundred thousand dollars

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:32.170
or something.

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:34.830
Every time a new person walks in the room

00:16:34.830 --> 00:16:39.100
with all their bags of
troubles, you're like, oh wow,

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:42.070
here's another one I can practice with

00:16:42.070 --> 00:16:44.890
and you feel like someone just
gave you a bag of diamonds

00:16:44.890 --> 00:16:45.723
or something.

00:16:45.723 --> 00:16:49.710
Like, wow, here's a new messed
up person I can be with.

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:52.890
And I'm so lucky.

00:16:52.890 --> 00:16:56.553
So that's called GCES SHING PHANGS

00:16:56.553 --> 00:17:00.990
GCES SHING PHANGS means the
person walks in the room

00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:05.120
with their bag of troubles
and you feel hungry

00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:11.770
to meet a new person that you can love.

00:17:11.933 --> 00:17:14.030
It's kind of cool.

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:15.330
That's the first one.

00:17:15.330 --> 00:17:19.900
Second one, BDE BA DANG
LDAN 'DOD KYI BYAMS PA GNYIS

00:17:19.900 --> 00:17:21.930
That's where the person walks in the room

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:26.040
with all their troubles,
you feel attracted to them

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:28.880
and you want to give them something.

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:33.847
Like that additional detail
is you want to share something

00:17:33.847 --> 00:17:37.460
with them or you want
to make them happier.

00:17:37.460 --> 00:17:41.563
You feel like you want to
give them some cool new thing.

00:17:42.755 --> 00:17:45.320
BYAMS PA GNYIS BYAMS PAR MTSUNGS

00:17:45.320 --> 00:17:48.560
BYAMS PAR MTSUNGS means, they're
both love, both are love.

00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:51.910
First one, where you just
see them as beautiful.

00:17:51.910 --> 00:17:55.210
Second, where you have
this overwhelming desire

00:17:55.210 --> 00:17:57.190
to give them something.

00:17:57.190 --> 00:17:58.937
Okay, they're both love, I know.

00:17:58.937 --> 00:18:03.490
KYANG but SPYI BYE BRAG LTA
BU'I KHYAD PAR CUNG ZAD YOD

00:18:03.490 --> 00:18:07.100
There's a little bit of
SPYI BYE BRAG going on here.

00:18:07.100 --> 00:18:09.513
Wow, what's that?

00:18:09.513 --> 00:18:11.852
What's SPYI BYE BRAG in a general sense?

00:18:11.852 --> 00:18:13.910
Here's a colloquial use

00:18:13.910 --> 00:18:17.290
of SPYI BYE BRAG, which you
can use later for emptiness.

00:18:17.290 --> 00:18:19.830
What is SPYI?

00:18:19.830 --> 00:18:22.672
General and then BYE BRAG is?

00:18:22.672 --> 00:18:24.600
(unclear)

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:27.240
Yeah, SPYI is like cars,

00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:29.740
and BYE BRAG is like Tesla.

00:18:29.740 --> 00:18:32.590
Which one of these two loves is the cars

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:36.393
and which one of these
two loves is the Tesla?

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:41.163
Don't forget, the first one was the person

00:18:41.163 --> 00:18:44.000
comes in the room and you are already

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:47.330
strongly attracted to them
because you can help them.

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:50.170
And then in the second one,

00:18:50.170 --> 00:18:53.170
you're dying to give them something.

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:55.333
Say again.

00:18:55.333 --> 00:18:57.800
[Student] It is cars.
[GMR] Yeah, good, yeah.

00:18:57.800 --> 00:19:02.410
Them coming in the room is SPYI, is cars.

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:06.252
And then the additional feature

00:19:06.252 --> 00:19:08.577
that you want to give them something

00:19:08.577 --> 00:19:09.942
is like BYE BRAG.

00:19:09.942 --> 00:19:14.200
That's a specialized
form of the general love.

00:19:15.513 --> 00:19:18.760
CUNG ZAD YOD means there's
a bit of a flavor that way.

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:20.670
It says, yeah, there's a
little flavor that way.

00:19:20.670 --> 00:19:22.430
If you can catch it,

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:25.740
you can go deeper in your study of love.

00:19:25.740 --> 00:19:29.230
And I would say, if you can
be sensitive to the parallel

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:33.045
in the two kinds of
compassion, that's very useful.

00:19:33.045 --> 00:19:36.069
YID 'ONG GI BYAMS PA NI MAR SHES DRIN DRAN

00:19:36.069 --> 00:19:38.469
DRIN GZO GSUM GYIS DRANGS SHING

00:19:38.469 --> 00:19:41.368
When we talk about beautiful love,

00:19:41.368 --> 00:19:44.221
which means when someone comes in the room

00:19:44.221 --> 00:19:48.600
and needs something, it seems
extremely attractive to you.

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:51.020
When we talk about that kind of love

00:19:51.020 --> 00:19:54.702
we're talking about the
love which was an automatic

00:19:55.670 --> 00:20:00.670
result of MAR SHES DRIN DRAN DRIN GZO.

00:20:00.780 --> 00:20:04.470
This has been my mom, she did this for me.

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.087
I want to pay her back.

00:20:06.087 --> 00:20:10.393
Then that should trigger the
first kind of the general love,

00:20:10.393 --> 00:20:14.530
SPYI love, where you're
attracted to the person.

00:20:14.530 --> 00:20:16.790
What about the BYE BRAG kind?

00:20:16.790 --> 00:20:20.497
DES SNYING RJE CHEN PO SKYED
PAR BYED PAS SNYING RJE

00:20:20.497 --> 00:20:23.281
CHEN PO'I SNGON DU NGES PAR 'GRO DGOS

00:20:23.281 --> 00:20:26.700
And by the way that general
love, where you feel attracted

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:30.100
to people is the one that you need

00:20:30.100 --> 00:20:32.840
to get to step number five.

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:36.570
That supposedly triggers compassion

00:20:36.570 --> 00:20:40.170
as one of the seven steps
in developing bodhichitta.

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:44.403
So in the scheme of the seven steps,

00:20:45.450 --> 00:20:48.210
the first kind of love,
the general kind of love,

00:20:48.210 --> 00:20:53.210
is important as a intermediate
step in the process.

00:20:53.447 --> 00:20:55.687
So what about the other kind of love?

00:20:55.687 --> 00:20:57.545
What was the other kind of love?

00:20:57.545 --> 00:20:58.828
You want to

00:20:58.828 --> 00:21:00.233
give them something.

00:21:00.233 --> 00:21:02.870
BDE BA DANG PHRAD 'DOD KYI BYAMS PA

00:21:02.870 --> 00:21:07.624
This is called
I-want-them-to-bump-into-happiness love.

00:21:07.624 --> 00:21:09.835
PHRAD means bump into.

00:21:09.835 --> 00:21:11.610
It's a cute name.

00:21:11.610 --> 00:21:14.765
It means you want to give them something.

00:21:14.765 --> 00:21:16.749
BDE BA DANG PHRAD 'DOD KYI BYAMS PA

00:21:16.749 --> 00:21:18.782
DANG SNYING RJE LA RGYU 'BRAS GO RIM

00:21:18.782 --> 00:21:21.757
Now think about it. He says

00:21:22.600 --> 00:21:25.800
general love, where you
find people to be beautiful

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:30.800
because they need you,
that always triggers

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:34.857
compassion, where you want
to pull them out of the fire.

00:21:34.857 --> 00:21:36.880
But,

00:21:36.880 --> 00:21:40.330
that relationship between
compassion and the love

00:21:40.330 --> 00:21:45.320
which wants to give something
to people can go both ways.

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:46.880
That's his point.

00:21:46.880 --> 00:21:51.010
It could be that wanting
to give them something

00:21:51.010 --> 00:21:54.210
leads you to want to
get them out of trouble,

00:21:54.210 --> 00:21:56.830
or it could be they're wanting
to get them out of trouble

00:21:56.830 --> 00:21:59.342
leads you to want to give them something.

00:21:59.342 --> 00:22:03.210
And he says, that's the difference
and it's a little subtle.

00:22:03.210 --> 00:22:06.176
And I got to say, it's such a pleasure,

00:22:07.060 --> 00:22:09.260
I mean, how many places in the world,

00:22:09.260 --> 00:22:12.610
how many rooms in the world right now

00:22:12.610 --> 00:22:16.910
are people discussing,
which compassion came first

00:22:16.910 --> 00:22:19.377
or the love came first, and
which kind of love came first

00:22:19.377 --> 00:22:21.765
and which kind of comparison came before,

00:22:21.765 --> 00:22:23.463
which kind of love?

00:22:23.463 --> 00:22:26.900
I say, boy, we are so
lucky to be in a room

00:22:26.900 --> 00:22:29.730
where someone is debating

00:22:29.730 --> 00:22:34.370
how to love people better.

00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:36.660
I'm saying to study Lam Rim,

00:22:36.660 --> 00:22:40.090
to live with the scriptures,
is a beautiful life.

00:22:40.090 --> 00:22:42.223
It's an extraordinarily beautiful life.

00:22:42.223 --> 00:22:45.378
We're not talking about
which democrat you're going

00:22:45.378 --> 00:22:47.230
to vote for, or republican.

00:22:47.230 --> 00:22:49.122
We're not talking about

00:22:49.122 --> 00:22:51.172
which Netflix film is better.

00:22:51.172 --> 00:22:53.583
We're talking about, what kind of love

00:22:53.583 --> 00:22:55.720
should I try to get first, Geshe-la?

00:22:55.720 --> 00:22:57.657
I heard this one might be better

00:22:57.657 --> 00:23:00.075
but I'm thinking the other one might.

00:23:00.075 --> 00:23:03.408
Just to have the discussion is an honor.

00:23:10.181 --> 00:23:14.974
LAM RIM CHEN MOR DRIN GZO'I
MJUG THOGS DER BDE BA DANG

00:23:14.974 --> 00:23:18.430
PHRAD 'DOD KYI BYAMS PA
BSGOM TSUL GSUNGS PA LTAR

00:23:18.430 --> 00:23:22.510
In the great Lam Rim of Tsongkapa

00:23:22.510 --> 00:23:24.935
DRIN GZO'I MJUG THOGS DER

00:23:24.935 --> 00:23:26.867
after you

00:23:28.100 --> 00:23:32.520
practice wanting to pay back your mom,

00:23:32.520 --> 00:23:35.530
you should go straight to the kind of love

00:23:35.530 --> 00:23:37.520
where you want to give them something.

00:23:37.520 --> 00:23:39.058
That's the Lam Rim.

00:23:39.058 --> 00:23:40.853
That's Tsongkapa's position.

00:23:40.853 --> 00:23:44.095
BSGOM TSUL GSUNGS PA
LTAR 'GA' ZHIG LA DE LTAR

00:23:44.095 --> 00:23:46.344
SNYING RJE'I SNGON DU
BSGOM NA'ANG RUNG MOD

00:23:46.344 --> 00:23:48.125
He says yeah, but some people say

00:23:48.125 --> 00:23:49.692
you could switch the order.

00:23:49.692 --> 00:23:52.060
You could do compassion first.

00:23:52.060 --> 00:23:54.453
If you don't get a person out of trouble,

00:23:54.453 --> 00:23:57.991
how can they enjoy the
candy you give them?

00:23:57.991 --> 00:24:00.605
So there's a difference in the loves.

00:24:00.605 --> 00:24:03.670
I like this picture of...

00:24:07.300 --> 00:24:11.780
I always found it was easier
to think about it this way.

00:24:11.780 --> 00:24:15.590
There's a school of
Buddhist thought that says,

00:24:15.590 --> 00:24:17.750
come on,

00:24:17.750 --> 00:24:21.320
if the kid falls down off the bicycle

00:24:21.320 --> 00:24:22.790
and cuts their arm,

00:24:22.790 --> 00:24:25.570
your first job is to put
something on the arm.

00:24:25.570 --> 00:24:28.740
Then your second job is to
give them a piece of candy.

00:24:28.740 --> 00:24:32.360
Don't give them a piece of candy

00:24:32.360 --> 00:24:35.390
before you fix their
cut. Fix the cut first,

00:24:35.390 --> 00:24:37.080
then give them the candy.

00:24:37.080 --> 00:24:39.473
Compassion should come before love,

00:24:39.473 --> 00:24:43.282
especially the love that
wants to give candy.

00:24:43.282 --> 00:24:46.390
SKYONG TSUL MAN NGAG LUGS
LTAR BYED NA BDE BA DANG

00:24:46.390 --> 00:24:49.665
PHRAD 'DOD KYI BYAMS PA
SNYING RJE'I RJES SU BSGOM

00:24:49.665 --> 00:24:52.807
SKYONG TSUL MAN NGAG LUGS LTAR

00:24:52.807 --> 00:24:55.220
means there's a oral tradition

00:24:55.220 --> 00:24:58.936
and he's going to contradict
the LAM RIM CHEN MO,

00:24:58.936 --> 00:25:00.850
the big Lam Rim.

00:25:00.850 --> 00:25:04.473
He's going to say, look,
there's a tradition that

00:25:04.473 --> 00:25:07.122
BDE BA DANG PHRAD 'DOD
KYI BYAMS PA SNYING RJE'I

00:25:07.122 --> 00:25:08.839
RJES SU BSGOM

00:25:08.839 --> 00:25:12.810
First, do the compassion
and then do the love

00:25:12.810 --> 00:25:15.093
where you want to give them something.

00:25:15.093 --> 00:25:16.517
You can do it this way.

00:25:16.517 --> 00:25:18.463
DE NAS LHAG BSAM LA 'JUG PA YIN PAS

00:25:18.463 --> 00:25:20.054
That will take you naturally

00:25:20.054 --> 00:25:22.968
into taking responsibility for them.

00:25:22.968 --> 00:25:24.918
DE LTAR NA BDE BA DANG LDAN
'DOD KYI BYAMS PA GTZO BOR

00:25:24.918 --> 00:25:26.459
MTSAMS 'DIR BSGOM ZHING

00:25:26.459 --> 00:25:29.713
Therefore, my recommendation,
Pabongka Rinpoche,

00:25:29.713 --> 00:25:32.610
let's focus in this section,

00:25:32.610 --> 00:25:34.240
on the kind of love where you want

00:25:34.240 --> 00:25:35.580
to give something to them,

00:25:35.580 --> 00:25:37.627
you want to share something with them,

00:25:37.627 --> 00:25:41.287
because that's a good one
to go into responsibility.

00:25:41.287 --> 00:25:45.144
LAM RIM CHEN MO'I SA BCAD
LTAR, SNYING RJE'I SNGON DU'ANG

00:25:45.144 --> 00:25:47.052
YID 'ONG GI BYAMS PA
DANG SBRAGS NAS CUNG ZAD

00:25:47.052 --> 00:25:48.311
BSAM DGOS GSUNGS,

00:25:48.311 --> 00:25:52.137
But he said, if you want to
do it like the big Lam Rim,

00:25:52.137 --> 00:25:55.777
like Tsongkapa's Lam Rim,
SNYING RJE'I SNGON DU'ANG

00:25:55.777 --> 00:25:58.713
you could do love before compassion,

00:25:59.570 --> 00:26:04.040
or SBRAGS NAS means you
could kind of combine them

00:26:04.040 --> 00:26:05.740
at the same time.

00:26:05.740 --> 00:26:07.377
And that would be okay.

00:26:07.377 --> 00:26:09.118
SBRAGS means combine.

00:26:09.118 --> 00:26:10.809
CUNG ZAD BSAM DGOS

00:26:10.809 --> 00:26:13.258
You guys think about it, he
said. You guys think about it.

00:26:13.258 --> 00:26:14.520
Think about it a bit.

00:26:14.520 --> 00:26:19.130
It means it will be
profitable for you spiritually

00:26:19.130 --> 00:26:21.690
if you figure this out yourself.

00:26:21.690 --> 00:26:25.410
Should you worry first
about the pain people have

00:26:25.410 --> 00:26:27.490
and then worry about their happiness?

00:26:27.490 --> 00:26:29.430
Or should do you worry
about their happiness first

00:26:29.430 --> 00:26:31.150
and then think about their pain?

00:26:31.150 --> 00:26:34.070
Or is there some way you can mix it up?

00:26:34.070 --> 00:26:37.863
Probably everything is
profitable spiritually.

00:26:37.863 --> 00:26:41.420
LHAG BSAM, we're on to number six.

00:26:41.420 --> 00:26:44.178
The six of the seven steps to

00:26:45.377 --> 00:26:47.380
reaching this bodhisattva vision.

00:26:47.380 --> 00:26:51.480
Step number one: see that
they have been your mother.

00:26:51.480 --> 00:26:54.730
Number two: think about

00:26:54.730 --> 00:26:56.802
all the good stuff they did for you.

00:26:56.802 --> 00:26:59.760
Number three: think
about paying them back.

00:26:59.760 --> 00:27:03.100
Number four: have love for them.

00:27:03.100 --> 00:27:05.690
Number five: have compassion for them.

00:27:05.690 --> 00:27:10.130
And now LHAG BSAM, which
means you take responsibility.

00:27:10.130 --> 00:27:15.130
There's an American president,
Harry Truman, 1950 something,

00:27:16.790 --> 00:27:20.700
and he had a sign on his desk
that said the buck stops here.

00:27:20.700 --> 00:27:22.610
And that sign is very famous.

00:27:22.610 --> 00:27:25.710
It means all the problems come to me

00:27:25.710 --> 00:27:27.368
and I don't pass them on.

00:27:27.368 --> 00:27:28.872
They have to be decided here.

00:27:28.872 --> 00:27:30.440
I'm the last one in the line.

00:27:30.440 --> 00:27:32.460
I'm the president.

00:27:32.460 --> 00:27:35.750
Problems come up, come up,
come up through the government.

00:27:35.750 --> 00:27:36.910
Then they reach here,

00:27:36.910 --> 00:27:39.820
and then I understand
I have responsibility.

00:27:39.820 --> 00:27:43.070
I'm the last person who
has to make decisions.

00:27:43.070 --> 00:27:44.980
And he said,

00:27:44.980 --> 00:27:48.780
I accept the responsibility.
I take, I understand,

00:27:48.780 --> 00:27:50.790
I understand all the serious problems

00:27:50.790 --> 00:27:53.610
will reach this office
and then they can't go out

00:27:53.610 --> 00:27:55.452
of this office to somebody else.

00:27:55.452 --> 00:27:56.647
I have to choose.

00:27:56.647 --> 00:27:59.812
I have to make decisions, hard decisions.

00:27:59.812 --> 00:28:03.790
DRUG PA LHAG BSAM NI, MA'I
KHUR BU LA BABS PA BZHIN

00:28:03.790 --> 00:28:07.800
Look in the end, if someone gave you birth

00:28:07.800 --> 00:28:12.730
and brought you up, then the
problem of taking care of them

00:28:12.730 --> 00:28:14.720
is yours.

00:28:14.720 --> 00:28:18.230
And this is famous with every generation

00:28:18.230 --> 00:28:21.980
of humans that ever lived.
We all have to think

00:28:21.980 --> 00:28:26.007
who's going to take care of
my mom when she gets old?

00:28:26.007 --> 00:28:29.190
And in the end, there's
one person. It's you.

00:28:29.190 --> 00:28:30.023
Why?

00:28:30.023 --> 00:28:32.020
Because she's your mom, okay?

00:28:32.020 --> 00:28:34.932
So pretty simple but
still a lot of Americans

00:28:34.932 --> 00:28:36.675
have trouble with it.

00:28:37.515 --> 00:28:41.035
BABS PA BZHIN, SEMS CAN THAMS CAD KYI

00:28:41.035 --> 00:28:43.820
I have a diamond dealer,
close spiritual friend

00:28:43.820 --> 00:28:48.210
in India, and he built
a room for his father

00:28:49.130 --> 00:28:52.073
onto his apartment,

00:28:53.080 --> 00:28:56.700
and he wiped his father's
bottom for many years.

00:28:56.700 --> 00:28:59.190
The father was senile.

00:28:59.190 --> 00:29:01.290
He would sit there in the bed

00:29:01.290 --> 00:29:03.220
and my friend would wash him every night,

00:29:03.220 --> 00:29:04.730
clean up his poo poo every night.

00:29:04.730 --> 00:29:07.560
And they live like that for years

00:29:07.560 --> 00:29:11.843
and they built that
special room just for him.

00:29:12.968 --> 00:29:16.495
LHAG BSAM NI, MA'I KHUR
BU LA BABS PA BZHIN

00:29:16.495 --> 00:29:19.170
KHUR means the burden of
taking care of the mom

00:29:19.170 --> 00:29:21.224
always should fall to the children.

00:29:21.224 --> 00:29:24.657
SEMS CAN THAMS CAD KYI
SDUG BSNGAL SEL BA DANG,

00:29:24.657 --> 00:29:28.006
BDE BA THAMS CAD SGRUB
PA'I KHUR RANG GIS KHYER

00:29:28.006 --> 00:29:31.250
Therefore, the responsibility
for everyone's happiness

00:29:31.250 --> 00:29:35.100
and to stop everyone's
pain has fallen to us

00:29:35.100 --> 00:29:39.050
because we're kids and
they're our mom. Don't forget.

00:29:39.050 --> 00:29:42.593
So don't try to avoid your
natural responsibility.

00:29:43.514 --> 00:29:46.555
KHUR RANG GIS KHYER NAS
SANGS RGYAS KYI SA LA BDAG

00:29:46.555 --> 00:29:48.289
RANG GIS 'GOD

00:29:48.289 --> 00:29:53.289
Therefore I will drag
myself to enlightenment.

00:29:53.700 --> 00:29:57.410
Building the extra room
onto your apartment

00:29:57.410 --> 00:30:01.748
means how to take care of your mom.

00:30:01.748 --> 00:30:04.077
I got to get to enlightenment first

00:30:04.077 --> 00:30:06.840
and then I'll be capable
to take care of my mom.

00:30:06.840 --> 00:30:09.920
That's how you take care of your mom.

00:30:09.920 --> 00:30:14.330
Don't focus on feeding
and cleaning your mom.

00:30:14.330 --> 00:30:16.330
Focus on getting to enlightenment

00:30:16.330 --> 00:30:18.700
and then you can really
take care of your mom.

00:30:18.700 --> 00:30:21.570
It doesn't mean you don't
have to clean your mom,

00:30:21.570 --> 00:30:24.900
but it means in the end

00:30:24.900 --> 00:30:28.840
your motivation should be,
I want to get to Buddhahood

00:30:28.840 --> 00:30:32.505
so I can really help my
mom because that's my duty.

00:30:32.505 --> 00:30:33.964
That's my natural duty.

00:30:33.964 --> 00:30:36.090
RANG GIS 'GOD CES THAG BCAD PA NI

00:30:36.090 --> 00:30:37.240
THAG BCAD PA NI

00:30:37.240 --> 00:30:39.078
means make up your mind.

00:30:39.078 --> 00:30:42.450
Like, stop being wishy-washy,
make up your mind.

00:30:42.450 --> 00:30:45.141
Look, we've been going
through all these steps

00:30:45.141 --> 00:30:47.950
for bodhichitta. Just decide.

00:30:47.950 --> 00:30:50.600
Yeah, those are my mom. - Okay.

00:30:50.600 --> 00:30:53.173
So you got to take care of her. - How?

00:30:53.173 --> 00:30:56.936
You got and get to Buddhahood
as fast as you can.

00:30:56.936 --> 00:30:59.994
That's the son and
daughter's responsibility.

00:30:59.994 --> 00:31:02.727
NYAN RANG LAS LHAG PA'I BSAM PA STE

00:31:02.727 --> 00:31:04.950
And then he explains LHAG BSAM

00:31:04.950 --> 00:31:07.133
which is very interesting.

00:31:08.370 --> 00:31:13.370
I looked up the Sanskrit is adhyashaya,

00:31:13.545 --> 00:31:17.110
adhyashaya,

00:31:17.110 --> 00:31:21.852
which means to have a superior thought.

00:31:21.852 --> 00:31:26.259
LHAG PA here like LHAG
MTHONG, vipashyana, it means a

00:31:26.259 --> 00:31:31.256
higher level of thinking
is adhyashaya, LHAG BSAM.

00:31:33.020 --> 00:31:35.683
And then he makes a joke,
Pabongka Rinpoche says,

00:31:37.590 --> 00:31:41.978
LHAG than who? Adhi than who?

00:31:41.978 --> 00:31:45.040
It's supposed to be,

00:31:45.040 --> 00:31:48.340
it's supposed to be a higher
kind of thinking process.

00:31:48.340 --> 00:31:51.280
Higher than who? Xan you guess?

00:31:51.280 --> 00:31:53.231
For $50?

00:31:54.440 --> 00:31:58.640
Higher than the two

00:31:58.640 --> 00:31:59.973
lower tracks.

00:31:59.973 --> 00:32:02.061
$50 for Tim.

00:32:02.061 --> 00:32:02.894
Jigme,

00:32:02.894 --> 00:32:04.585
$50 for Mr. Tim.

00:32:06.330 --> 00:32:08.060
Oh no, that's your job.

00:32:08.060 --> 00:32:10.340
They'll cheat us.

00:32:10.340 --> 00:32:13.620
They'll say they didn't make it.

00:32:13.620 --> 00:32:14.453
Yeah.

00:32:16.100 --> 00:32:18.718
He got $25 for self-made buddhas

00:32:18.718 --> 00:32:21.011
and $25 for listeners.

00:32:22.130 --> 00:32:25.680
So LHAG BSAM LHAG PA'I BSAM PA STE,

00:32:25.680 --> 00:32:29.790
So he explained the LHAG in LHAG BSAM,

00:32:29.790 --> 00:32:31.815
which means

00:32:32.800 --> 00:32:36.120
special responsibility
and what it means is

00:32:36.120 --> 00:32:40.847
more special than a
non-bodhisattva practitioners.

00:32:40.847 --> 00:32:44.090
And you won't see LHAG BSAM
ever explained like that.

00:32:44.090 --> 00:32:46.947
And you have to be
sensitive that he's doing it

00:32:46.947 --> 00:32:48.957
because he doesn't announce it.

00:32:48.957 --> 00:32:50.540
All right.

00:32:51.410 --> 00:32:54.397
I like to call it the
majesty of responsibility.

00:32:54.397 --> 00:32:56.273
I have a picture.

00:32:59.145 --> 00:33:01.212
Okay Geshe-la, what the heck?

00:33:01.212 --> 00:33:04.153
I mean this is supposed to be some person

00:33:04.153 --> 00:33:07.470
taking responsibility
for a whole civilization

00:33:07.470 --> 00:33:10.870
and you got a lady throwing
a bottle in a garbage can.

00:33:10.870 --> 00:33:12.700
Yeah. Why?

00:33:12.700 --> 00:33:15.700
She took responsibility for the planet

00:33:15.700 --> 00:33:17.530
in a small, personal way.

00:33:17.530 --> 00:33:20.340
She took responsibility for the planet

00:33:20.340 --> 00:33:22.055
in a small, personal way.

00:33:22.055 --> 00:33:24.520
I used to drink a lot of fizzy water

00:33:24.520 --> 00:33:28.493
in from, what's that place, Fiji,

00:33:29.510 --> 00:33:33.711
and my friend Pachi
said, Geshe-la come on,

00:33:33.711 --> 00:33:35.540
that's lame.

00:33:35.540 --> 00:33:37.980
You're stealing water
out of this tiny island

00:33:37.980 --> 00:33:41.760
and shipping in a jet
airplane through the sky,

00:33:41.760 --> 00:33:45.030
burning fuel the whole way
to get it to you in Sedona.

00:33:45.030 --> 00:33:46.230
Come on.

00:33:46.230 --> 00:33:49.220
So this lady took responsibility

00:33:49.220 --> 00:33:51.130
and she didn't ask anybody.

00:33:51.130 --> 00:33:53.570
She didn't announce it to anybody.

00:33:53.570 --> 00:33:56.680
I liked to think that she picked up

00:33:56.680 --> 00:33:59.142
a plastic bottle on the street

00:33:59.142 --> 00:34:01.172
and she put it in the garbage can.

00:34:01.172 --> 00:34:02.920
And that's called

00:34:02.920 --> 00:34:07.050
glorious majesty of responsibility.

00:34:07.050 --> 00:34:09.150
She is a queen at that moment.

00:34:09.150 --> 00:34:14.150
She's more queen than those
guys running around in London.

00:34:14.700 --> 00:34:16.290
She's more of a queen.

00:34:16.290 --> 00:34:19.236
She's throwing out the plastic bottle.

00:34:21.223 --> 00:34:23.840
She bent over and picked
up the plastic bottle

00:34:23.840 --> 00:34:26.234
and put it in the garbage because

00:34:26.234 --> 00:34:28.380
she's taking quietly, anonymously,

00:34:28.380 --> 00:34:30.861
she's taking responsibility.

00:34:30.861 --> 00:34:34.410
DPER NA, MI ZHIG G-YANG
DU LHUNG BA MTHONG BA

00:34:34.410 --> 00:34:38.384
MA BZOD NAS DE 'DON
MKHAN BYUNG NA CI MA RUNG

00:34:38.384 --> 00:34:42.910
means if you see somebody fall off a ship

00:34:42.910 --> 00:34:46.170
into the Pacific Ocean

00:34:46.170 --> 00:34:49.860
and you're at the rail,
you know like Titanic.

00:34:49.860 --> 00:34:53.380
And you're like, oh I
hope someone grabs him.

00:34:53.380 --> 00:34:56.617
I hope someone can get to him.

00:34:56.617 --> 00:34:57.970
You know, like, oh,

00:34:57.970 --> 00:35:00.150
I hope so bad that someone saves him.

00:35:00.150 --> 00:35:02.490
Or what's going to happen next?

00:35:02.490 --> 00:35:05.203
You jump.

00:35:05.203 --> 00:35:08.187
RUNG SNYAM PA LTA BU NI
BYAMS PA SNYING RJE GNYIS

00:35:08.187 --> 00:35:09.786
DANG MTSUNGS SHING

00:35:09.786 --> 00:35:12.820
That is kind of love and
that is kind of compassion.

00:35:12.820 --> 00:35:17.044
But DE LTAR MA BZHAG PAR RANG
GIS 'DON RGYUR BLO THAG BCAD

00:35:17.044 --> 00:35:18.600
BLO THAG BCAD

00:35:18.600 --> 00:35:22.220
means make the god damned decision.

00:35:22.220 --> 00:35:24.910
Somebody has to jump off the
Titanic and grab this person.

00:35:24.910 --> 00:35:27.173
It's going to be me.

00:35:27.173 --> 00:35:29.152
That's called THAG BCAD PA

00:35:29.152 --> 00:35:31.320
It's a beautiful verb in Tibetan.

00:35:31.320 --> 00:35:34.120
It means the buck stops here.

00:35:34.120 --> 00:35:36.600
I'm not going to look to somebody else.

00:35:36.600 --> 00:35:38.880
Oh, somebody fell off the boat.

00:35:38.880 --> 00:35:43.330
You have to find a staff
person to try to help them.

00:35:43.330 --> 00:35:46.410
No - THAG BCAD PA

00:35:46.410 --> 00:35:48.330
means you don't talk to anybody,

00:35:48.330 --> 00:35:52.780
just god damn take off your
shirt and jump in the water

00:35:52.780 --> 00:35:54.270
and go after them.

00:35:54.270 --> 00:35:56.095
That's THAG BCAD PA.

00:35:57.277 --> 00:36:00.993
LHAG BSAM DANG 'DRA BAS,
that's personal responsibility.

00:36:00.993 --> 00:36:05.219
SPYIR BYAMS PA DANG SNYING RJE
TZAM NYAN RANG LA YOD KYANG

00:36:05.219 --> 00:36:08.350
Generally speaking,
non-bodhisattvas can have feelings

00:36:08.350 --> 00:36:10.940
of compassion and love for other people,

00:36:10.940 --> 00:36:13.870
but, KYANG, LHAG BSAM, no,

00:36:13.870 --> 00:36:15.760
they don't have it.

00:36:15.760 --> 00:36:17.190
They are not going to say,

00:36:17.190 --> 00:36:19.770
I'm the person who's jumping off the ship.

00:36:19.770 --> 00:36:22.620
Unless you're on the bodhisattva track,

00:36:22.620 --> 00:36:25.380
you're going to look
around for a staff member

00:36:25.380 --> 00:36:28.320
and let them know somebody
fell out the boat.

00:36:28.320 --> 00:36:30.400
If you're on the bodhisattva track,

00:36:30.400 --> 00:36:32.323
you're going to LHAG BSAM.

00:36:32.323 --> 00:36:34.440
You're going to say, oh wow, so cool,

00:36:34.440 --> 00:36:37.300
it came down to me. I'm the one.

00:36:37.300 --> 00:36:39.600
I got to, I got to jump now.

00:36:39.600 --> 00:36:43.040
So, all right, and we've all
been in those situations.

00:36:43.040 --> 00:36:46.570
If you get to my age,
you been in situations

00:36:46.570 --> 00:36:50.310
where you have to make a quick decision.

00:36:50.310 --> 00:36:52.984
Either I risk my life or
I wait for somebody else.

00:36:52.984 --> 00:36:54.810
And then you just,

00:36:54.810 --> 00:36:59.340
it's nice if you have this,

00:36:59.340 --> 00:37:01.460
if you're able to feel LHAG BSAM

00:37:01.460 --> 00:37:03.983
and say, okay, it's
down to me, let's do it.

00:37:04.930 --> 00:37:06.340
It's a very beautiful thing.

00:37:06.340 --> 00:37:08.510
You feel very proud of yourself later

00:37:08.510 --> 00:37:12.830
that you didn't look for a staff person.

00:37:12.830 --> 00:37:15.530
I'm telling you it's one
of the pleasures of life.

00:37:15.530 --> 00:37:20.454
LHAG BSAM 'DI DANG DRIN GZO'I
SKABS KYI KHUR KHYER LUGS

00:37:22.980 --> 00:37:26.610
So somebody asks a question
to Pabongka Rinpoche.

00:37:26.610 --> 00:37:29.420
You're talking about taking
responsibility, right?

00:37:29.420 --> 00:37:31.112
- Yeah.

00:37:31.112 --> 00:37:35.500
How does that differ from the third step?

00:37:40.700 --> 00:37:43.473
Where you want to

00:37:43.473 --> 00:37:45.930
DRIN GZO, pay them back.

00:37:45.930 --> 00:37:48.925
What's the difference
between step number six

00:37:48.925 --> 00:37:50.758
and step number three?

00:37:53.140 --> 00:37:56.870
Well, step number three
is I'll pay my mom back.

00:37:56.870 --> 00:37:59.100
She took care of me, I'll pay her back.

00:37:59.100 --> 00:38:01.512
And what's the difference between that

00:38:01.512 --> 00:38:05.770
and step number six,
where you say it's on me?

00:38:05.770 --> 00:38:08.970
He says, you tell me the difference.

00:38:08.970 --> 00:38:10.670
Here he answers

00:38:10.670 --> 00:38:15.670
DPER NA TSONG PAS NOR RDZAS
NYO BAR BRTZOM PA DANG

00:38:15.940 --> 00:38:18.320
You are in tje department store,

00:38:18.320 --> 00:38:23.320
you see a beautiful dress,
and you're like, man.

00:38:24.780 --> 00:38:29.780
I remember I was in Taiwan.
I went to Christian Dior.

00:38:29.790 --> 00:38:33.338
They had a $3,000, sorry,
they had a nice dress

00:38:33.338 --> 00:38:36.240
and I thought I'm going
to buy that for Veronica.

00:38:36.240 --> 00:38:39.870
I stood there for like 20 minutes

00:38:39.870 --> 00:38:42.837
and I said, "God that's one
of the most beautiful dresses

00:38:42.837 --> 00:38:44.150
I ever seen."

00:38:44.150 --> 00:38:46.790
And then I asked the lady,
how much is the dress?

00:38:46.790 --> 00:38:49.943
And she said $3,000 or $5,000
and I'm like [drops jaw].

00:38:51.240 --> 00:38:54.560
And then you have this moment,

00:38:54.560 --> 00:38:56.990
are you going to jump on not?

00:38:56.990 --> 00:39:01.290
By the way, I did not,
but maybe I should have.

00:39:01.290 --> 00:39:04.020
But I thought it was too much.

00:39:04.020 --> 00:39:07.360
But in that moment you
have a decision to make.

00:39:07.360 --> 00:39:09.295
Are you going to jump or not?

00:39:09.295 --> 00:39:12.880
So, normal compassion,

00:39:12.880 --> 00:39:14.900
normal love,

00:39:14.900 --> 00:39:18.260
is like admiring the dress.

00:39:18.260 --> 00:39:22.630
And then the difference
between that and LHAG BSAM,

00:39:22.630 --> 00:39:25.531
the difference between that
and taking responsibility is?

00:39:25.531 --> 00:39:30.450
Yeah, here's the credit card, god damn.

00:39:30.450 --> 00:39:33.290
Here's the god damn credit card.

00:39:34.180 --> 00:39:36.600
By the way, I didn't do it.

00:39:36.600 --> 00:39:40.400
I mean, I did it in another place and

00:39:41.730 --> 00:39:44.680
she ended up giving the
dress to Peter and Marija

00:39:44.680 --> 00:39:47.420
for her wedding because
it was so beautiful.

00:39:47.420 --> 00:39:50.800
She said, there is a
wedding dress, Geshe-la.

00:39:50.800 --> 00:39:52.166
And anyway,

00:39:53.400 --> 00:39:56.080
it's an interesting
distinction for Pabongka,

00:39:56.080 --> 00:39:59.090
who's not supposed to
be engaged in business.

00:39:59.090 --> 00:40:02.590
We read that in the monk's vows
last term in the Mixed Nuts.

00:40:02.590 --> 00:40:06.090
He's like, it's like when you take out

00:40:06.090 --> 00:40:08.770
your god damn credit card,
put it down on the counter.

00:40:08.770 --> 00:40:12.230
I'm up for it . I'm there.

00:40:12.230 --> 00:40:13.860
Here's my credit card.

00:40:13.860 --> 00:40:16.230
Okay, so think about it.

00:40:16.230 --> 00:40:19.122
It's an interesting
analogy for a monk to make.

00:40:20.155 --> 00:40:22.130
TSONG THAG BCAD PA

00:40:22.130 --> 00:40:24.291
means you decide.

00:40:24.291 --> 00:40:26.407
BZHIN GYI BLO THAG BCAD PA

00:40:26.407 --> 00:40:28.308
means you make that decision.

00:40:28.308 --> 00:40:30.039
You jump. You jump.

00:40:30.039 --> 00:40:32.010
MA BCAD PA'I KHYAD PAR YIN

00:40:32.010 --> 00:40:35.076
If you don't jump yet,
that's number three.

00:40:36.130 --> 00:40:38.670
I would like to pay her back.

00:40:38.670 --> 00:40:41.820
And if you do jump it's number six.

00:40:41.820 --> 00:40:43.683
I'm going to pay her back.

00:40:43.683 --> 00:40:46.360
Got it? Cool?

00:40:46.360 --> 00:40:49.175
ZHES BLA MA RIN PO CHE GSUNG

00:40:49.175 --> 00:40:52.416
BLA MA RIN PO CHE GSUNG means
my teacher taught me that,

00:40:52.416 --> 00:40:54.991
said our teacher.

00:40:54.991 --> 00:40:59.241
So he's crediting it to,
what's his teacher's name?

00:41:00.140 --> 00:41:02.550
Who wrote the...

00:41:02.550 --> 00:41:05.134
SBYOR LAM

00:41:07.003 --> 00:41:09.310
SBYOR CHOS, he wrote the SBYOR CHOS.

00:41:09.310 --> 00:41:11.030
Anyway, you can check.

00:41:11.030 --> 00:41:12.517
I always forget his name,

00:41:12.517 --> 00:41:14.250
Pabongka Rinpoche's teacher.

00:41:14.250 --> 00:41:16.160
He said that's what my teacher said.

00:41:16.160 --> 00:41:18.778
Oh so maybe his teacher was buying horses

00:41:18.778 --> 00:41:22.020
and stuff, I don't know.

00:41:23.070 --> 00:41:26.870
And I like the picture here,

00:41:28.130 --> 00:41:30.120
this guy's calling his mom,

00:41:30.120 --> 00:41:31.725
"Okay, I bought my first building,

00:41:31.725 --> 00:41:35.138
like I jumped, you know, I
signed the mortgage just now."

00:41:35.138 --> 00:41:36.470
The building's behind him.

00:41:36.470 --> 00:41:40.090
I remember when we bought our
first building in New York

00:41:40.090 --> 00:41:42.030
and it was a big gamble.

00:41:42.030 --> 00:41:43.470
It was a big risk.

00:41:43.470 --> 00:41:47.240
We waffled for a couple months

00:41:47.240 --> 00:41:49.820
and then we said, god damn let's do it,

00:41:49.820 --> 00:41:52.110
and that feeling in your heart like,

00:41:52.110 --> 00:41:54.150
okay, god damn, I'm there,

00:41:54.150 --> 00:41:56.978
I'm going to buy it.

00:41:56.978 --> 00:41:59.320
I think that he's like

00:41:59.320 --> 00:42:03.243
that guy in New York, 1990-something,

00:42:04.801 --> 00:42:07.433
who said, okay, mom,
I bought the building.

00:42:07.433 --> 00:42:09.490
I made the decision.

